[size=4][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]
Settings and logs are in [i]bin\x64\Braindance3D[/i] (logs go to [i]%LOCALAPPDATA%\Braindance3D[/i] if the game folder is read-only).
[list]
[*][b]Crash or no start after installing or a game update:[/b] disable the mod and report your game version.[/*]
[*][b]3D Mode greyed out:[/b] check RED4ext and read [i]Braindance3D-autosetup.log[/i]. With several monitors, set [i]Monitor = primary[/i] in [i]Braindance3D-Settings.ini[/i] and play on it.[/*]
[*][b]Menus look wrong:[/b] set [i]Squeeze = off[/i] in the [i]Menus[/i] section of the settings file and report with [i]Braindance3D-hooks.log[/i].[/*]
[*][b]No DLSS in the game's Frame Generation list with OptiScaler:[/b] set [i]FGInput = nofg[/i] and [i]FGOutput = nofg[/i] in [i]OptiScaler.ini[/i] (with [i]FGOutput = DLSSG[/i], OptiScaler holds DLSS-G even with [i]Enabled = false[/i], so the game drops DLSS from its list).[/*]
[*][b]Depth inside out:[/b] use your viewer's swap-eyes option.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Known limitations[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Overlays drawn over the game look split in 3D (fine in 2D): Cyber Engine Tweaks' overlay during gameplay (fine over a game menu, so pause before opening it), and OptiScaler's own menu and FPS counter always. To use them, turn 3D Mode off in the game's settings; it switches live, with no restart. [i]FpsOverlayPos = 0[/i] keeps OptiScaler's counter readable in the left eye.[/*]
[*]Mod Organizer 2 isn't supported yet.[/*]
[*]Untested: multi-monitor setups, viewers other than Virtual Desktop.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Bugs[/b][/size]
Use the Bugs tab or [url=https://github.com/vl3c/cyberpunk2077-3d-braindance-edition/issues]GitHub issues[/url]. Include game version and store, GPU, how you view the 3D, and the logs ([i]braindance3d.log[/i], [i]Braindance3D-autosetup.log[/i], [i]Braindance3D-hooks.log[/i]) with [i]Level = 2[/i] in the settings file. Logs contain folder paths, which can include your Windows user name.

